cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "GUI to ADCP Docking"
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it and the docking engine it runs.
  ADCP (AutoDock CrankPep) and ADFRsuite were developed by the Scripps
  Research Institute and are not part of this work; this package is a
  browser and command-line workflow that runs them. The full citation list
  for a run, including the preparation and rescoring tools it used, is
  printed by `adcp-dock cite <run>`.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Aadhil
    family-names: Haq
    affiliation: "HOPE Lab, Texas A&M University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8335-2121"
  - given-names: Sandun
    family-names: Fernando
    affiliation: "HOPE Lab, Texas A&M University"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7692-2170"
    role: "Principal Investigator"
version: "0.1.5"
license: "MIT"
abstract: >-
  Browser and command-line workflow for ADCP peptide docking. It connects
  receptor preparation, grid generation, docking, optional MM-GBSA
  rescoring and reporting, and runs on a Slurm cluster, a local computer or
  Google Colab.
keywords:
  - peptide docking
  - ADCP
  - molecular docking
  - MM-GBSA
  - high-performance computing
references:
  - type: article
    title: >-
      AutoDock CrankPep: combining folding and docking to predict
      protein-peptide complexes
    authors:
      - family-names: Zhang
        given-names: Yuqi
      - family-names: Sanner
        given-names: Michel F.
